---
title: honey zaatar baked butter beans
servings: 2
prep-time: 5 minutes
cook-time: 25 minutes
tags: [high-protein, recipe, beans, high-fibre, snack]
source: https://www.instagram.com/reel/DSVnf8bkpAR/
image: https://scontent-iad3-2.cdninstagram.com/v/t51.82787-15/601176965_18000004877845139_7386574152125351633_n.jpg?stp=cmp1_dst-jpg_e35_s640x640_tt6&_nc_cat=106&ccb=7-5&_nc_sid=18de74&efg=eyJlZmdfdGFnIjoiQ0xJUFMuYmVzdF9pbWFnZV91cmxnZW4uQzMifQ%3D%3D&_nc_ohc=yJ8ryZ1Paa4Q7kNvwG9iZaY&_nc_oc=Adlpyvd4YZpv7d6aVRDNaoNxndh2oP1fjEfYwCVSR8d8NpUFFrVXeRlgYRAUxLIOVT4&_nc_zt=23&_nc_ht=scontent-iad3-2.cdninstagram.com&_nc_gid=SZ0nBFAFDDdInuxv-FVKcA&oh=00_AfkCtchfgyAg-XNOTPt-Ib3w6MM63F8jhSNqFWBg6pQuCA&oe=695693EA
---

Preheat your #oven to 400°F. In a #bowl{}, combine @butter beans{1%can} with @olive oil{1%tbsp}, @honey{1%tbsp}, @za'atar{1%tbsp}, and @salt{1%tsp} to coat the beans evenly.

Spread the coated beans on a #baking sheet{} in a single layer and roast in the preheated oven for ~{25%minutes}, until the edges are crisp and the centers are tender. Stir halfway through to promote even browning, then return to the oven to finish cooking. Serve warm.